+# FAA transcript certifications, revised times and a recorded correction shipment
+
+**Six newly acquired official NARA PDFs now supply the signed-certification scans and a concrete correction-dispatch record behind the earlier timing comparison.** All **23 pages** were visually inspected; the original **641,090 bytes** are preserved unchanged. The records advance a version/custody inquiry. They do **not** supply the corrected May 2003 Commission answer, proof of its delivery or the signed administrative action/no-action decision.
+
+The strongest new comparison is that a December 3, 2001 Henderson Radar transcript and a May 7, 2002 Radar Associate transcript agree on six selected command/check-in times while differing from earlier compilation pages. One additional repeated-call pair differs by a second. These are printed-source observations, not accepted historical clock measurements. No preferred time or explanation is selected.
+
+## Sources, scope and locators
+
+| ID | Official catalog and released scan | Pages; SHA-256 |
+|---|---|---|
+| S01 | [ZID93, AAT-200 request note](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596630) | 1; `8f20feb7c28f2e0e9e56bfbea4edb7fd1515e30f15e4cf5842b2b3f4bc92b9d8` |
+| S02 | [ZID166, Certified Index](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596481) | 1; `713a5438f6d9b49d1fa4235c5993c7fc41257e62934942bd6735544b55bf2329` |
+| S03 | [ZID158, no-splicing note](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596478) | 1; `4e93a60dcb3d77020c48ddd2e57c74d748d5e214f99bf6c947e46143a7e7a5d1` |
+| S04 | [ZID161, Henderson Radar partial transcript](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7595834) | 5; `6c304d1a27a2ae34951e2883182a3f1fc2ec682258061e9de6512fc79aa19d99` |
+| S05 | [ZID162, Henderson Radar Associate partial transcript](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7595835) | 13; `1a6252be9720f383377310b07e876e1e95173b198ce9b5a1a5cb21e6e581f2e0` |
+| S06 | [ZID105, corrected-record dispatch email and sender airbill](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596426) | 2; `162d54edeb6ebe6394ea71e3bd1dd8f61d3ecbb1b1195d7e02c6ae3b1e9bda1e` |
+
+[SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) records exact download URLs, access times, lengths, source qualifications and the prior F04/NAID7596179 pin. New source IDs are local to this unit. The earlier [F04 version review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ca224c35d97a1aac5d885e8a85bc76fc3d08a037/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-package-version-review-2026-10-27/README.md) remains unchanged.
+
+Page references are one-based PDF pages. Extracted line references in [EXCERPTS.json](EXCERPTS.json), [COMPARISONS.json](COMPARISONS.json) and [QUALIFIER-COMPARISONS.json](QUALIFIER-COMPARISONS.json) use **PyMuPDF sorted-text extraction for this unit**; they are not original agency line numbers or interchangeable with a different extraction's line order. All acquired page images were inspected, separately from software/diff checks. Official hosting, a hash and a scanned signature do not independently authenticate the historical assertion or a native signing event. Raw scans, full extractions, signatures, names/contact details and airbill identifiers remain local; no concealed fields were reconstructed or used.
+
+## C01 — What the index and certifications actually say
+
+**S02, p1**, dated **December 3, 2001**, certifies that the listed copies are true copies of originals on file in the office. It lists **14 record categories**, including original voice recordings, certified cassette rerecordings, partial transcripts, DART, NTAP, SAR tapes and SATORI. Fourteen categories are not fourteen physical items, a complete delivered manifest or proof the underlying originals survive today. The index does not itself provide the voices/data or identify their byte-level relationships. Selected text: p1, lines6–24.
+
+**S04, p1** is a December 3, 2001 memorandum for the Henderson Radar position, covering **1234–1309 UTC**. **S05, p1** is dated May 7, 2002 for the Radar Associate position, covering **1234–1320 UTC**. Each bears a signature image and language certifying a true transcription of recorded conversations pertaining to the accident. S04 p1, lines19–20,29–30; S05 p1, lines9–10,18–19,32–33.
+
+These are explicit documentary certification claims with different preparation dates and position/window labels. They are not independent measurements merely because there are two signatures or positions. A true-transcription assertion is not automatically a complete-master, selected-channel, copy-generation or historical-clock certification. Both records are called **Partial Transcript**.
+
+## C02 — Preserve all four printed versions of the selected times
+
+The existing six candidate events were selected by flight/words/context before this unit. Their association is not established by an original event ID. F04 p71–72 explicitly says DRAFT and bears September 13, 2001 fax markings; F04 p38 is an annotated associate-position page. The fax label is not a verified composition or dispatch date.
+
+| Candidate event | F04 p38 associate page | F04 p71–72 radar draft | S04 p2, Dec3 transcript | S05 p2/p4, May7 transcript |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Check-in | 1240:14 | 1240:14 | 1240:13 | 1240:13 |
+| Squawk instruction | 1240:16 | 1240:16 | 1240:15 | 1240:15 |
+| Climb instruction | 1243:52 | 1243:52 | 1243:51 | 1243:51 |
+| Climb readback | 1243:54 | 1243:54 | 1243:55 | 1243:55 |
+| Right-vector instruction | 1247:20 | 1247:20 | 1247:16 | 1247:16 |
+| Ten-right readback | 1247:33 | 1247:23 | 1247:20 | 1247:20 |
+
+The **compiled associate minus December** differences are **+1,+1,+1,−1,+4,+13 seconds**. The **radar draft minus December** differences are **+1,+1,+1,−1,+4,+3 seconds**. A single constant offset does not reproduce either six-row set. This is a narrow arithmetic result conditional on the candidate joins; it does not measure the recorder's historical clock, establish a deliberate revision, or determine which value is correct.
+
+The six selected December and May values agree. Conversely, the second short Indy call in the page-local 1256 sequence is **1256:46 in S04 p3** and **1256:45 in S05 p4**. Thus these seven declared cross-position pairs yield **six zero differences and one +1-second difference**, with S04 minus S05 as the sign convention. This is a selected comparison, not a census of every utterance or independent corroboration.
+
+The ten-degree instruction/readback also appears in the newly acquired versions. The earlier F04 p52 chronology's **20-degree instruction / 10-degree acknowledgment**, and all other prior values, remain preserved. Newer certification wording is not being used to adjudicate that conflict. Required next inputs: actual source channels, master/copy mapping, timecode-reader records, transcript drafts/change logs and the reason for each selected revision.
+
+## C03 — Relay qualification survives, but the printed times and some entry classifications differ
+
+The newly acquired S05 retains the **unconfirmed** impact report and later attributed **confirmed** relay. It therefore preserves the earlier question about how certainty was conveyed; it does not newly supply an independent source confirming the impacts.
+
+| Candidate entry | Earlier F04 | S05 May7 transcript |
+|---|---|---|
+| First unconfirmed report | p45,1309:05 | p9,1309:05 |
+| Repeated unconfirmed report | p45,1309:27 | p9,1309:29 |
+| Relay attributing confirmation | p45,1310:34 | p10,1310:39 |
+| Subsequent attributed confirmation | p46,1311:30 | p11,1311:27 |
+| Boston answer | p47,1314:45 | p12,1314:43 |
+
+The first-report-to-relay subtraction is **89 seconds in F04** and **94 seconds in S05**. Neither is an independently calibrated historical elapsed-time measurement. The original 89-second finding is retained with its own source, not overwritten by 94.
+
+At the same printed **1313:54**, F04 p47 says **override line beeping**, while S05 p11 says **(unintelligible)**. At **1314:04**, F04 p47 says **line ringing**, while S05 p11 again says **(unintelligible)**. These are observable wording/classification differences; they do not establish an absent audio interval, splice or suppressed physical event. Actual recordings, transcription conventions, version notes and connected-channel context are needed. The original utterance and certainty-change cause remain unresolved.
+
+## C04 — A recorded correction dispatch, with receipt and content still unverified
+
+**S06 p1**, printed **5/9/02,8:42AM**, reports that the last AAL77 corrections were FedExed to ZDC on **5/8/02**. Its list comprises personnel logs, position logs, **three transcripts** and **19 personnel statements**. These are reported shipment categories/counts, not acquired copies of all contents or nineteen independent witnesses.
+
+The writer reports surprise at the receiving end that the requested personnel/position logs were being sent. The note also says **hold out for partial transcripts**. Preserve that wording and the affirmative dispatch account together. The phrase's exact negotiation/selection meaning, the scope of the underlying request and the reason for each correction are not established by this email. It is not sufficient to infer that substantive speech was deliberately concealed.
+
+**S06 p2 is the sender's airbill copy**, not a delivery scan or recipient signature. Its date field displays **5/8/02** beneath a struck earlier date that appears to read **4/30/02**; the earlier handwriting reading is qualified. Both are retained as a low-weight form/version observation without inferring backdating or selecting a reason. The tracking identifier is preserved in the original locally but not republished.
+
+The May7 transcript date and the May8 dispatch claim are a candidate association, not proof that S05 was one of the three enclosed transcripts. A versioned enclosure list, actual transmitted copies, hashes or other identifying correspondence and receiving acknowledgment are still needed. This 2002 dispatch is also **not the missing corrected May2003 QFR or proof of a 2006 recommendation outcome**.
+
+## C05 — Preserve contrary instructions and limit the AAT-200 association
+
+**S03 p1** visibly says **Do not splice AAL77 or UAL93**. The short note has no verified author/date or execution record. It documents an instruction against splicing; it does not prove all source or derivative tapes complied, nor support a claim that this note orders splicing. The poor text layer is not a reliable transcription of its large handwriting.
+
+**S01 p1** is headed **AAT-200 REQ**, with **9/11** and marginal **9/12** markings and a checklist covering voice/rerecording and operational supporting records. No complete year/author/native routing is authenticated. It does not itself establish the later 2003 release restriction reported in AWA661, much less the correction or administrative outcome under PD01–PD04. An identical office code alone cannot join different requests across years.
+
+## Methods, failures and remaining work
+
+[compare_sources.py](compare_sources.py) reproduces the selected timestamp comparisons from the seven exact pinned PDF entities; [REPRODUCIBILITY.json](REPRODUCIBILITY.json) records actual results and limits. Its **event selection** uses words and surrounding sequence while retaining raw extracted text. It does not normalize original time values or infer the physical clock.
+
+An initial script assertion found no exact match for the search cue roger squawk because the older PDF text layer misreads that visible word. The failure and first script remain local; the executed version instead uses the same utterance's preceding phrase **indy center roger**, still requiring one unique source match. No timestamp or source byte was changed, and the unique-match requirement was not waived. A separate initial preparation command used a Python environment without PyMuPDF and failed at import before writing output; the existing correct runtime was then used without installation. These are our processing limitations, not suspicious source findings.
+
+All 23 newly acquired page images were inspected. All new originals and the held F04 match their recorded hashes. These controls verify preservation and the declared comparison, not historical truth or goal completion. [Checklist](CHECKLIST.md) and [open originals](OPEN-RECORDS.md) retain every substantive dependency.
+
+The strongest alternative to a wrongdoing interpretation is that these are openly labeled drafts, later partial transcripts, ordinary copy/correction activities and different recording positions. Their ordinary potential explanations do not erase the differences. Conversely, discrepancies and a correction shipment do not establish intentional falsification. No cause, motive or controlling historical value is selected.
+
+**Still open:** actual May2003 corrected QFR and receipt; signed administrative consideration/action/no-action decision; recommendation-disposition/implementation/closure records; native recordings and clock/copy/version joins; and the telephone, raw-recorder, matched-specimen materials and steel-attribution requirements in the full work plan. No new request, outreach, fee, private-case publication, private push, deletion, source overwrite, history rewrite or case-spine edit occurred in this research unit.
